From 6cd179ae4248b6b76d82a4f9036c4618dced662a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Feb 2026 10:15:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 440/572] fix(psci): check error value for
 psci_find_target_suspend_lvl

If psci_find_target_suspend_lvl() returns PSCI_INVALID_PWR_LVL which is
an error in psci_system_suspend, the function should exit with
PSCI_E_DENIED. Update the return check conditions.
This was found with Coverity analysis (overrun logic_error).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git f952674cde358737cfc917bb7d936cbe2a20c62d fix(psci): check error value for psci_find_target_suspend_lvl]
Change-Id: Ic3abc8844038523a9a0d1daad8d2676d2058d377
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/541289
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
---
 lib/psci/psci_main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/psci/psci_main.c b/lib/psci/psci_main.c
index a4dd240358..1ad19a16c3 100644
--- a/lib/psci/psci_main.c
+++ b/lib/psci/psci_main.c
@@ -191,7 +191,7 @@ int psci_system_suspend(uintptr_t entrypoint, u_register_t context_id)
 	 * (System level)
 	 */
 	pwrlvl = psci_find_target_suspend_lvl(&state_info);
-	if (pwrlvl < min_pwrlvl) {
+	if ((pwrlvl == PSCI_INVALID_PWR_LVL) || (pwrlvl < min_pwrlvl)) {
 		return PSCI_E_DENIED;
 	}
 	/* Ensure that the psci_power_state makes sense */
-- 
